# Dependencies
#
# BOTH forms, and the second is not redundant. A pattern with a trailing slash
# matches only a real DIRECTORY, so `node_modules/` alone does not ignore a
# node_modules SYMLINK -- and a symlink is what you get whenever somebody links
# a worktree at the primary checkout's install to avoid a second npm ci.
# Measured: with only the slash form, `git check-ignore node_modules` reports
# no match for a symlink and `git status` lists it as untracked, so `git add -A`
# stages it. That is exactly how branch claude/book-toc-titletoc came to commit
# node_modules as a symlink to the absolute path /home/user/port-daddy/node_modules,
# which resolves on one machine and is silently broken everywhere else.
node_modules/
node_modules

# Database
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Logs
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Build output
# Slash-less twins, for the same symlink reason as node_modules above: a linked
# `dist` or `target` is a directory to the developer and a plain symlink to git.
dist/
dist
**/target/
**/target
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# LaTeX intermediates, repo-wide.
#
# PREVENTIVE -- this untracks nothing. Zero .aux/.toc/.fls/.fdb_latexmk/.synctex.gz
# files are tracked today, and scripts/build-whitepapers.sh keeps its
# intermediates in .cache/whitepaper-build, which `.cache/` already covers.
#
# The gap it closes is a hand-run build. Two TeX source trees carry their own
# ignore file -- website-v2/public/whitepaper/ and whitepaper/ -- and
# docs/harbor-research/ (19 .tex sources, 37 figure sources, built in CI by
# harbor-research-build.yml) carries none. Running latexmk there by hand drops a
# dozen intermediates beside the sources with nothing watching, and TeX
# byproducts are the kind of thing that gets committed once and lives forever.
#
# `.out` is deliberately NOT here: unlike the rest it is not TeX-specific, and a
# repo-wide `*.out` would quietly swallow genuine fixtures. No .out file is
# tracked today either, so the rule would be speculative in both directions.
*.aux
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# Test coverage
coverage/

# TLC model checker intermediate state (only check in .tla, .cfg, .run.log)
proofs/**/states/

